  "where": "cast › small"
 },
 {
  "id": "p150",
  "en": "Age the voice first",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p151",
  "en": "A small shift in formant, pitch and pace makes a voice older. ElevenLabs steps in only when that falls short.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p152",
  "en": "Problem",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › small"
 },
 {
  "id": "p153",
  "en": "Accents disappeared",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p154",
  "en": "ElevenLabs Multilingual v2 kept them, but the lines came out flat.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p155",
  "en": "Fix",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › small"
 },
 {
  "id": "p156",
  "en": "Describe the accent in the voice",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p157",
  "en": "Gemini's designed voices take it from the prompt: Busan, Jeolla, Gyeongju, Tokyo, Hanoi, Melbourne.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p158",
  "en": "Problem",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › small"
 },
 {
  "id": "p159",
  "en": "Short replies sounded read out alone",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p160",
  "en": "A dry <span lang=\"ko\">그건 인정.</span> came out flat every time.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p161",
  "en": "Fix",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › small"
 },
 {
  "id": "p162",
  "en": "Voice the whole exchange",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p163",
  "en": "Then keep only the reply, so it sounds like an answer.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p164",
  "en": "Every new voice gets a test line before its episode is voiced.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "cast › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p165",
  "en": "QA for Korean pronunciation",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › h2"
 },
 {
  "id": "p166",
  "en": "Korean is written one way and said another. AI voices sometimes read the spelling.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › p.big-p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p167",
  "en": "Every language does this. In English, \"handbag\" sounds like \"hambag\".",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p168",
  "en": "Nasalisation",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › small"
 },
 {
  "id": "p169",
  "en": "<span class=\"w\" lang=\"ko\">국물</span><span class=\"ar\">said as</span><span class=\"s\" lang=\"ko\">궁물</span>",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › div.pair"
 },
 {
  "id": "p170",
  "en": "said as",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › span.ar"
 },
 {
  "id": "p171",
  "en": "ㄱ softens to ㅇ before ㅁ.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p172",
  "en": "Palatalisation",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › small"
 },
 {
  "id": "p173",
  "en": "<span class=\"w\" lang=\"ko\">같이</span><span class=\"ar\">said as</span><span class=\"s\" lang=\"ko\">가치</span>",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › div.pair"
 },
 {
  "id": "p174",
  "en": "said as",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › span.ar"
 },
 {
  "id": "p175",
  "en": "ㅌ before 이 becomes ㅊ, like \"gotcha\".",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p176",
  "en": "Tensing",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › small"
 },
 {
  "id": "p177",
  "en": "<span class=\"w\" lang=\"ko\">똑바로</span><span class=\"ar\">said as</span><span class=\"s\" lang=\"ko\">똑빠로</span>",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › div.pair"
 },
 {
  "id": "p178",
  "en": "said as",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › span.ar"
 },
 {
  "id": "p179",
  "en": "ㅂ hardens to ㅃ after ㄱ.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p180",
  "en": "Respell what the voice reads",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p181",
  "en": "Rules rewrite each sentence as it's said before voicing. Learners still see the normal spelling.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p182",
  "en": "Find the gap in QA",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p183",
  "en": "Speech-to-text checks spelling, not sound, so pronunciation needed its own check.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p184",
  "en": "Test three ways",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p185",
  "en": "Same sentence, three spellings, two engines. All sounded alike, so the models mostly know the rules.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p186",
  "en": "Fix what's left",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p187",
  "en": "Slips came across word gaps in long takes, like <span lang=\"ko\">고객 문의</span>. Now risky phrases are joined, numbers are spelled out, and Claude reviews each script before voicing.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p188",
  "en": "One shared pronunciation tool for cards and podcast, with zero re-voicing costs.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "pronunciation › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p189",
  "en": "Review ops: one sheet, blockers first",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › h2"
 },
 {
  "id": "p190",
  "en": "By Level 3, my reviews lived across three separate pages.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › p.big-p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p191",
  "en": "I folded them into one sheet, sorted by the day each decision is due. Anything that stops an episode from voicing turns red and moves to the top.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p192",
  "en": "Focus",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › span.tile-k"
 },
 {
  "id": "p193",
  "en": "I review audio only",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p194",
  "en": "Claude settles the script notes. I judge what needs ears.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p195",
  "en": "Decisions",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › span.tile-k"
 },
 {
  "id": "p196",
  "en": "Three answers per voice",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p197",
  "en": "Pass keeps the Gemini voice. Fail means I bring an ElevenLabs voice. Depends gives Gemini one more direction.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › p"
 },
 {
  "id": "p198",
  "en": "Checks",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › span.tile-k"
 },
 {
  "id": "p199",
  "en": "A voice print on every line",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › b"
 },
 {
  "id": "p200",
  "en": "It flags any line read in the wrong voice. The first run caught 11 lines in 20 episodes.",
  "kind": "html",
  "where": "review › p"
 },
 {
